      "body": "# WAFCON 2026: Malawi Beat Ghana to Reach Historic Semi-Finals, Betting Tips Ghana\n\nMalawi\u2019s stunning 2-1 victory over Ghana to reach the WAFCON 2026 semi-finals marks one of the most remarkable upsets in African women\u2019s football history. For Ghanaian bettors, this result reshapes the landscape of betting opportunities and strategies for the remainder of the tournament. This guide provides a detailed comparison of top bookmakers licensed by the Gaming Commission of Ghana (GCA), tailored betting tips for Ghanaian punters, and practical advice on how to navigate betting safely and smartly in Ghana\u2019s regulated market.\n\n## The Historic Upset: Malawi\u2019s Triumph Over Ghana\n\nThe Black Queens of Ghana entered the quarter-finals as favourites, but Malawi\u2019s resilience and tactical discipline earned them a 2-1 win at the Al Medina Stadium in Rabat. This victory not only secured Malawi\u2019s first-ever WAFCON semi-final berth but also qualified them for the 2027 FIFA Women\u2019s World Cup. For Ghanaian bettors, this unexpected outcome highlights the importance of analysing form, team dynamics, and underdog potential when placing bets.\n\n## Comparing Top Bookmakers for Ghanaian Bettors\n\nWhen betting on WAFCON 2026 matches, choosing the right bookmaker is crucial. Ghana\u2019s betting market is dominated by several GCA-licensed operators offering competitive bonuses, flexible payment methods, and reliable platforms. Here\u2019s a detailed comparison of three leading bookmakers:\n\n| Bookmaker       | Top Welcome Offer                          | Minimum Deposit | Payment Methods                                  |\n|-----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----------------|-------------------------------------------------|\n| Sportybet Ghana | 150% Welcome Bonus \u2013 Up to GH\u20b5500 Free Bet | GH\u20b51            | MTN MoMo, Vodafone Cash, AirtelTigo Money, Visa, Mastercard |\n| Betway Ghana    | 50% Welco